ession in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={2}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =13 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Phase for the Amplitude-Phase Form for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f31db222-f840-5886-aafa-4d2e070549fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299618} {:answer/id #uuid "01b1e251-99af-519d-8f84-58d19d2c36a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299619} {:answer/id #uuid "b77dd0b6-e1ea-5605-88bb-6fb938ff59f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299620} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb471e7-85b1-5c83-9cab-734d9c0a28aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299621} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7dbb93-11c7-5278-a984-b75e31c9ca4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :