\\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299623 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dba0779-e903-5281-bc41-01b78c31a98c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Amplitude for the Amplitude-Phase Form for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a8d7f8a-3c71-556b-8445-7aa7f3c7f447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299625} {:answer/id #uuid "56be5ad2-628d-58d3-8d53-104512895ae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299626} {:answer/id #uuid "0656043c-f0c7-5b23-bee4-d9720cdf4921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299627} {:answer/id #uuid "24f8d591-2c8d-573d-a01d-3527e59102a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299628} {:answer/id #uuid "0619e003-ff41-52d7-9812-d1306996dc22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0619e003-ff41-52d7-9812-d1306996dc22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299629} :answer-field/id #uuid "26d4b70d-234a-5b4e-8578-70b92b1bc20d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08e3efd6-39f9-56b1-8e11-679418895f9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80127" :question/problem "Given that the expression $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =9+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Phase for the Amplitude-Phase Form for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df9cb234-eed4-507c-9ec1-9e9aceafae02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276027} {:answer/id #uuid "c6843a56-169c-5c75-8868-e9c86cab9108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276028} {:answer/id #uuid "82f6df96-b111-5419-bd2a-259f3d9437cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276029} {:answer/id #uuid "4cfff3f8-100c-55a5-a281-9de36806e295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276030} {:answer/id #uuid "e9dbb64a-3cac-5b76-afcb-707ed66a1feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cfff3f8-100c-55a5-a281-9de36806e295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276030} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ed077ed-e31f-5fb4-aff3-0324418e805a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2482eaaf-f514-5577-a783-2f1ca414760f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80135" :question/problem "Given that the expression $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{5}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Amplitude-Phase Form for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe968fbe-d97d-504c-b62e-527278272744" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281895} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f0e66f-9dfb-5d78-b659-a4fae80d7f1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.156)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281896} {:answer/id #uuid "c74cb847-af86-546c-a94c-daee7590d07d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.854)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281897} {:answer/id #uuid "5df9f194-a06d-5fe6-a71d-aa94e6598893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.916)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281898} {:answer/id #uuid "79bca67a-6243-5257-b2e0-cd8c682f2588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.054)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe968fbe-d97d-504c-b62e-527278272744" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281895} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d3a0c80-1834-5558-a1e9-38a21bc6e1be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "da754d54-7ad0-5021-82bb-f04c6fa332b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-80147" :question/problem "$2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)≈$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =0.955\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =8+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =24 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)\n$$"}]}
